UID:WrkqN24USNf9lS9tNZbl5
SUMMARY:Paranoid Fantasies: World-Building in Conspiracy Narratives
DTSTAMP:20260805T053722Z
DTSTART:20260812T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  Speaker: Megan Oakes  Doctoral Candidate  Thesis Defen
	se  Department: English  This dissertation demonstrates how speculative na
	rratology can be brought to bear on the study of conspiracy theories by pe
	rforming a series of case studies of fantasy texts\, outlining how both fa
	ntasy and conspiracy narratives participate in a form of speculative world
	-building. This project also illustrates the connection between fantastic 
	aesthetics and conspiracy theorizing— specifically as a response to moment
	s of crisis and the narrative mechanisms that are employed in order to ref
	rame catastrophe as a punishable action.  &#160\;  (Department : English)\
	n\nhttps://events.rice.edu/live/events/435996-paranoid-fantasies-world-bui
	lding-in-conspiracy
URL:https://events.rice.edu/live/events/435996-paranoid-fantasies-world-bui
	lding-in-conspiracy
